course: dictionary
lesson: 16106
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning an author means by reading the words around it. «The little girl was weeping after she lost her teddy bear.» The sad story and the tears tell you that weeping means crying with tears.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another sentence. «Mia sat under the weeping willow by the pond.» A willow is a tree, so weeping here describes a tree whose branches hang down towards the ground. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one still makes sense. If a meaning sounds silly, try the next one. Good readers do this quickly, almost without noticing.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is right.
fact: «Weeping» means crying with tears, and it shows deep sadness in stories.
fact: «Weeping» can describe a tree whose branches hang down, like a weeping willow beside a river or pond.
fact: «Weeping» can also describe a wound or sore that lets out liquid, as in «a weeping wound».
fact: «Weeping» can be a noun meaning the sound or act of crying, as in «the weeping of the crowd».
exercise: «The little girl was weeping after she lost her teddy bear.» What does weeping mean? | Singing a happy song | Sleeping soundly | *Crying with tears | Laughing loudly
exercise: Mia sat under the weeping willow by the pond. What do the branches of a weeping willow do? | Turn bright red in summer | *Hang down towards the ground | Point straight up to the sky | Float on the water
exercise: «The doctor cleaned the weeping wound on his knee.» What does weeping mean here? | *Letting out liquid | Covered in a bandage | Very deep and dark | Healing very quickly
test: «The weeping in the hall went on for hours.» What does weeping mean here? | *The sound or act of crying | A kind of loud song | A tree with drooping branches | A wound that lets out liquid
test: «She was weeping quietly.» Which word could replace weeping in this sentence? | *Crying | Running | Shouting | Laughing
exam: Which sentence uses weeping to describe a tree? | She began weeping when the film ended. | The doctor cleaned the weeping cut. | *The weeping willow swayed over the pond. | The weeping boy dried his eyes.
